  {
   "id": "e-cA9MOZ2bEJ",
   "from": "John Harrison",
   "author": "a58a2a3609db3342",
   "date": "2014-04-03T17:35:58Z",
   "subject": "Re: Interacting with and testing Shiny apps using RSelenium",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">There is a new package rDVR to aid testing at <a href=\"https://github.com/johndharrison/rDVR\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/johndharrison/rDVR&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792401019578000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1Qdd_uWw0dZvEugMxSe3jy\">https://github.com/johndharrison/rDVR</a>.<br>The github page is at <a href=\"https://github.com/johndharrison/rDVR\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/johndharrison/rDVR&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792401019578000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1Qdd_uWw0dZvEugMxSe3jy\">https://github.com/johndharrison/rDVR</a>. There is a vignette on operation <h1>Recording R Sessions with rDVR: An example using RSelenium</h1>at <a href=\"http://rpubs.com/johndharrison/15176\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://rpubs.com/johndharrison/15176&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792401019578000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0pO7ofdU2E3OGtvNysKfKJ\">http://rpubs.com/johndharrison/15176</a>.<br>rDVR is a Cross Platform (Lin/Win/OSx) DVR for R allowing you to record your rsession with commands something like:<br><br><pre><code>require(rDVR)\nstartVServer() # utility function to start a video server\nDVR &lt;- rDVR()\nDVR$start()\n# Do your thing for upto 10 minutes\nDVR$save()\nDVR$closeServer()<br><br></code></pre>Comments and Suggestions welcome<br><br>Best Regards<br><br>John<br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "BKpXzuSzdJAJ",
   "from": "BadriNarayanan Srinivasan",
