   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi John -<div><br></div><div>I am very glad that I found your work. I am building web analytics audit tool using shiny and Rselenium, quick question, is that possible to capture the output of phantomexecute function in a variable in R?</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers,</div><div>Badri</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>On Thursday, April 3, 2014 6:35:58 PM UTC+1, John Harrison wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">There is a new package rDVR to aid testing at <a href=\"https://github.com/johndharrison/rDVR\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/johndharrison/rDVR&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792401019578000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1Qdd_uWw0dZvEugMxSe3jy\">https://github.com/johndharrison/rDVR</a>.<br>The github page is at <a href=\"https://github.com/johndharrison/rDVR\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/johndharrison/rDVR&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792401019578000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1Qdd_uWw0dZvEugMxSe3jy\">https://github.com/johndharrison/rDVR</a>. There is a vignette on operation <h1>Recording R Sessions with rDVR: An example using RSelenium</h1>at <a href=\"http://rpubs.com/johndharrison/15176\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://rpubs.com/johndharrison/15176&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792401019578000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0pO7ofdU2E3OGtvNysKfKJ\">http://rpubs.com/johndharrison/15176</a>.<br>rDVR is a Cross Platform (Lin/Win/OSx) DVR for R allowing you to record your rsession with commands something like:<br><br><pre><code>require(rDVR)\r\nstartVServer() # utility function to start a video server\r\nDVR &lt;- rDVR()\r\nDVR$start()\r\n# Do your thing for upto 10 minutes\r\nDVR$save()\r\nDVR$closeServer()<br><br></code></pre>Comments and Suggestions welcome<br><br>Best Regards<br><br>John<br></div></blockquote></div></div>"
